From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theo Slater <theoslater1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:26:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] RequestServer+LibRequests: Let the UI process ask how a host
 was reached

Browsers show the user how the connection to a secure site is secured:
its TLS version and cipher, and the certificate chain the server
presented. RequestServer now remembers these for each HTTPS host and
port it connects to, and the UI process asks for them with
RequestControlClient::retrieve_secure_connection(), which gives the
chain DER-encoded.

They are read from curl's OpenSSL handle once a response's headers
arrive, and only for a new connection, as a reused one presents what was
remembered for it already. Reading them takes references to the peer's
certificates, which are encoded only when the UI process asks. Asking
curl for CURLOPT_CERTINFO instead would make every connection collect
and format its certificates. The record also says whether the
connection was made over a certificate the user accepted although it
failed verification. RequestServer keeps the 128 hosts it last
connected to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
